      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-12-18_WidnesExaminer_art0002" n="art0002">
        <head>Church Notices.</head>
        <p>Church Notices.</p>
        <p>Vkr YCLIFFE CONGREGATIONAL CHURCH, BEWSEY-ST., WARRINGTON. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 19, 1915. Morning, 10.90: Rev. C. P. PITT, B.A. Evening, 6.30: CHRISTMAS CHORAL SERVICE. A. R. Gaul's Cantata: "THE PRINCE OF PEACE," • will be rendered by the Choir. Collection in aid of Choir Fund. P.S.A. FOR MEN, 3 P.m.</p>
        <p>BOLD-STREET WESLEYAN CHURCH. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 19th. 1030 a.m.: Rev. W. T. DERRY, M.A. 6.30 p.m.: SELECTIONS FROM HANDEL'S ORATORIO, "THE MESSIAH." Address by the Rev. PERCY INESON. SOLOISTS: . Soprano: Mrs. A. BOOTH Miss E. TAYLOR, Miss BROT.JOH, Miss i3LACKBURNE. Contralto: Miss WHITMORE, Miss KERSHAW. Tenor: Mr. J. CLAYTON, Mr. G. WILDE. Bass: Mr. E. H. PEARCE, Mr. W. WARBURTON. Organist: Mr. FRANK HICKMAN. Special Collections for Society Funds.</p>
        <p>13WSEY-ROAD WESLEYAN CHURCH. JLP TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 19th. 10.30 a.m.: Rev. P. INESON. 6.30 p.m.: SPECIAL CHORAL SERVICE. Selections from "THE MESSIAH:" Preacher: Rev. W. T. DERRY, "M.A.</p>
        <p>BAPTIST CHURCH, LATCHFORD. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 19th. Morning, 10.30. Evening, 6. Preacher: Mr. H. STOWELL, Manchester Baptist College.</p>
        <p>CAIRO-STREET CHAPEL, WARRINGTON . TO-MORROW (SUNDAY L DEC., lath.</p>
        <p>..Res;:—IRVINg LISTER. Morning, 10.30: "The Culture of the Soul." Evening, 6.30: "Fight fd,r Right."</p>
        <p>OHRISTADELPHIAN MEETING ROOM, BOLD-STREET, WARRINGTON.--Free Bibb!</p>
        <p>Address SUNDAY NEXT, at 6.30 p.m. Subject "Christ and the Prophets." Mr. W. S. FRITH, of Alderley Edge.</p>
        <p>FRIENDS' MEETING ROUSE, BUTTER- MARKET-STREET, WARRINGTON. DAVID P. BOYD, of Manchester, Will give an Address on "SACRIFICE AND SERVICE," TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), DECEMBER 19. 1915. At 6.30 o'clock. A Cordial Invitation to all. No Collection.</p>
        <p>GOLBORNE-STREET BAPTIST CHURCH. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 19th. Preacher: Rev. H. OGDEN. Morning 10.46. Evening, 6.30. CAROL SERVIaES and SELECTIONS from "THE MESSIAH." Evening Soloists: Miss Olive Dale, Miss Maude Jones and Mr. Arthur Pearce.</p>
        <p>PRIMITIVE METHODIST CHURCH, LEGH-STREET. WARRINGTON. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 19, 1915. Morning, 10.30. Evening, 6.30. Rev. T. A. YOUNG, of Widnes. Evening, 6.30: SPECIAL MUSICAL CAROL SERVICE. Soloists: Mrs. C. WORTHINGTON, MTS. A. E. HOYLE, Mr. J. DARIN. 48010 Violin: Mr. H. WOODLAND. Anthem. "Sweetly through the night" (Shelly). ST. JOHN'S PRESBYTERIAN CHURCH, WILDERSPOOL CAUSEWAY. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY). DEC. 19. 1915. Morning, 10.45. Evening. 6.30. Preacher: Rev. W. REID.</p>
