        <p>All Seats Free. Collection taken. WARRINGTON BLUE COAT CHARITY SCHOOL. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the Trustees of the above School will, at their next Quarterly, Meeting, on the 17th day of January next, pro- ceed to elect four Children (four Boys) to Vacancies now existing in the Institution. No Candidate will be eligible unless an application on his behalf (forms of which may be obtained from the Clerk, at his Office, 3, Winwick-stre6t), shall have been made to the Clerk to the Trustees at least fourteen days previous to the day of Meet- ing. In electing Children, the Trustees make Orphans their first choice. Those deprived of one parent come next in consideration, and after them the children of parents who have the greatest number and the slenderest means. Dated this 16th day of December. 1915. HENRY GREENALL, Clerk to the Trustees.</p>
        <p>LONDON CITY AND MIDLAND BANK, LIMITED, WARRINGTON.</p>
