      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-12-18_WidnesExaminer_art0137" n="art0137">
        <head>Warrington Help.</head>
        <p>Warrington Help.</p>
        <p>Mrs. E. Lawton, of 36, Marbury-street, Latchford, Warrington, says :—" I believe my kidney trouble was brought on by catch- ing a chill after having a bad back. I suffered terribly with my back after that. I was laid up for three weeks at a time, and the pain was so acute that I dared not turn from one side to the other. I was de- pressed and low-spirited, and seemed to have lost all my energy. The kidney excretions were unnatural and there as distress in 'relieving the bladder. " Doan's Backache Kidney Pills did nw good from the first, and after I had given the pills a fair trial I lost all the pain, the kidney weakness was corrected, and I felt like a new woman in health. I can recom- mend DOMIN Pills. because they did me so much good."</p>
        <p>(Signed) "E. Lawton."</p>
        <p>Be sure you ask for DOAN'S and get DOAN'S—the Pills Mrs. Lawton had.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-12-18_WidnesExaminer_art0138" n="art0138">
