        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. CLEANSING DEPARTMENT. IMPORTANT NOTICE AS TO THE USE OF ASHBINS. The. Corporation give notice that owing to the Shortage of men and horses in consequence of the war it has become neeesc.ary to curtail the iirdrk of tli removal Of Rouse Refuse, and house- holders are earnestly asked to assist' by all means.. in reducing the quantity of refuse to be removdd. Ashbins, as the name denotes, are intended only for ashes and dry refuse. Material, such as-fish heads, vegetable refuse, bad fruit, waste paper, should be burned in the kitchen grate. There is a chance that it may not always be possible to empty ashbins as regularly as in ordinary ,times. - It is essential therefore that the amount of waste refuse from each house should be limited as much as possible. By order of the Sanitary Works Committee. JAMES J. A; PARFITT, M.1.C.5., Cleansing Superintendent. December, 15th,, 1915. COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER. NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the next GENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the Peace for tile COUNTY PALATINE OF CHESTER will be holden at the CASTLE OF CHESTER, in and for the Said County, on MONDAY, the 3rd DAY OF JANUARY, 1916, at 11.30 o'clock, in the Forenoon, when the Grand Jury will be empannelled. The hearing of all 'Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions of Broxton? Chester Castle, Daresbury, Eddisbury, Nantwich, Run- corn,. Winsford, and Wirral. forming the Ches- ter District, and the trials of all prisoners com- mitted from the last-mentioned Divisions will take place at such Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Chester District must be in attendance at the CASTLE OF CHESTER, at the opening of the Court on MONDAY, the 31d DAY OF JANUARY, 1916 at 11.30 o'clock in the Forenoon. THE COURT will be Adjourned to the COURT HOUSE. KNUTSFORD, on WEDNES- DAY, the sth DAY OF JANUARY, 1916, at 10.30 o'clock in the Forenoon. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Petty Sessional Divisions of Altrincham, Buck- low, Dukinfield, Middleivich, 'Sandbach, Congle- ton, Northwich, Prestbury'and Stockport form- ing the Knutsford District, hnd the trials of all prisoners committed from such Divisions will take place at such Adjourned Sessions. The Grand and Petty Juries for the Knutsford Dis- trict must be in. attendance at the ,COURT HOUSE, KNUTSFORD, at the opening of the Court on . WEDNESDAY, the sth DAY OF JANUARY, 1916, at 10.30 o'clock in the Fore- noon. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Peace for the County Pdlatine of Chester. Chester, 17th Deeember, 1915.</p>
