        <p>MONEY TALKS. Iq Whilst it is clearly the duty of the Government to bring home to the community the facts Concerning the value of money during the present crisis, it is equally important that the community should take notice of the Government's Instructions. „ g The Special Response to the War Loan is evidence of the people's desire to help. There are thousands, however, who are making more wages at the present time than they ever made before, or are likely to make in the future, and who have not yet realised the necessity for saving. If each worker will set aside his extra earnings and deposit them in the Savings Bank, he will not only .be helping to. provide "silver bullets." to beat the - Germans, but he will be making It easier for himself, his wife and children, to overcome the slump in trade when the War is over. I q If you have a Savings Bank Account, and know that you can withdraw a little money when it is needed, it vill make your life happier and give you an independence which tile person in debt never has, or can hope to have. It is quite true that money "talks." At your service: THE WARRINGTON, RUNCORN AND DISTRICT SAVINGS BANK. I Established 1818. I Head Office BUTTERNIARKET STREET. Branches BANK QUAY: 29, Green Street. EARLESTOWN : 5' Queen Street. - Runcorn Office 40, HIGH STREET. _</p>
